      "body": "## Purpose\n\n`tests/v1/shutdown` intermittently fails on Intel CI (XPU) with `Failed: Timeout (>120.0s) from pytest-timeout`, e.g. in various `tensor_parallel_size=2` cases of `test_forward_error.py`/`test_startup_error.py` (see https://buildkite.com/vllm/intel-ci/builds/14158, 14130, 14120).\n\nXPU forces the `spawn` multiprocessing start method instead of `fork` (see `vllm/platforms/xpu.py`), which means every EngineCore/Worker subprocess re-imports the whole package and re-initializes the device runtime, instead of inheriting it via `fork`'s copy-on-write memory. That is noticeably slower and more variable than CUDA's fork-based startup, so the fixed 120s `SHUTDOWN_TEST_TIMEOUT_SEC` budget intermittently trips before the subprocesses finish starting, especially with `tensor_parallel_size=2`.\n\n## Changes\n\nRaise `SHUTDOWN_TEST_TIMEOUT_SEC` to 240s on XPU, keep the 120s budget unchanged for other platforms.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nRan the affected suite on XPU hardware:\n\n```\npython -m pytest tests/v1/shutdown/test_startup_error.py -k \"forward-2\" -v\n```\n\n## Test Result\n\n```\ntests/v1/shutdown/test_startup_error.py::test_async_llm_startup_error[forward-2-hmellor/tiny-random-LlamaForCausalLM] PASSED\n1 passed, 7 deselected in 47.53s\n```\n\nConfirmed via `pytestmark` introspection that the effective timeout marker is now 240s on XPU. `ruff`/`pre-commit` pass.\n\n---\n\nAI assistance (GitHub Copilot CLI) was used to investigate the Buildkite failures and draft this change; I reviewed the diff and ran the tests above myself.",
